{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>What has it profited?</b> It serves another, and thus he says to the king of the Chaldeans, when the cup of HaShem's right hand turns upon you — what has the idol profited?" "<b>Its maker</b> is the artisan who forms it, and what has the molten image profited?" "<b>And a teacher of lies</b> is a priest of idolatry — all these, what have they profited you?! And one may wonder, for surely its maker fashioned it upon it to make mute idols — the meaning is, the form of a man: they have a mouth but do not speak."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:52.952584614Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}